<!--
Xbox Series S|X controller over Bluetooth (045e:0b13, BLE).

Driver: xpadneo v0.10.5 (DKMS, XPADNEO_REF). core.c sets vendor 0x045E, product
0x028E and version 0x1130 for EVERY supported controller ("pretending XB1S Windows
wireless mode"). So SDL sees 045e:028e and not 0b13, and this file has the same
nodes as xboxone-bt.xml. Buttons from mappings.c, axes from events.c. The name is
the Bluetooth name of the controller. Without xpadneo (DKMS failed, see the build
report) hid-generic handles the pad with the real ID and other button codes. SDL then
names 045e:02fd "Xbox One S Controller" and 045e:0b13 "Xbox Series X Controller", the
same deviceName as in the USB templates. The GUID does not match, so ES matches by
name, loads the USB mapping and the buttons are WRONG (no wizard appears). The web
UI "reset" does not help (it matches the GUID or the kernel name "Xbox Wireless
Controller", es_input.cfg has neither). Then connect a USB keyboard (ES has a
built-in default keyboard mapping) and use the ES menu "Configure Input" for the
pad; or fix xpadneo and rebuild. Or, via SSH, remove the inputConfig node with
this deviceName from ~/.emulationstation/es_input.cfg and restart ES.

Buttons (SDL joystick index = evdev key codes in ascending order, BTN_JOYSTICK and up first):
  A (south) 0, B (east) 1, X (west) 2, Y (north) 3, LB 4, RB 5, Back 6, Start 7,
  Guide 8, left stick 9, right stick 10.
Axes: left stick 0/1, LT 2, right stick 3/4, RT 5. D-pad: hat 0.
xpadneo puts Share on a separate keyboard device; ABS_PROFILE is axis 6 (not used).

deviceName is the SDL joystick name, as EmulationStation writes it. ES looks for
the GUID first and then for deviceName (InputManager::loadInputConfig), so the
name is the fallback when the version in the GUID differs (spec section 9).
The CRC in the GUID is computed from the kernel name (see guid-source).
SDL names 045e:028e "Xbox 360 Controller" (controller_list.h).

GUID with CRC (SDL 2.26 and newer, as on bookworm) and without CRC
(older SDL), computed with "emulationstation-web guid" from these values:
guid-source: bus=0x05 vendor=0x045e product=0x028e version=0x1130 name="Xbox Wireless Controller"

UNVERIFIED - check on hardware: without xpadneo the pad gets the USB mapping by
  name (wrong buttons, no wizard), see above.
UNVERIFIED - check on hardware: Bluetooth (BLE) name "Xbox Wireless Controller" and the BLE connection
  through BlueZ (HID over GATT).
UNVERIFIED - check on hardware: ES writes the SDL name "Xbox 360 Controller" (not the kernel name) as deviceName
  on bookworm (SDL 2.26 or newer).

Sources:
  https://github.com/atar-axis/xpadneo/tree/v0.10.5/hid-xpadneo/src/xpadneo (core.c, mappings.c, events.c)
  https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL/tree/release-3.2.10/src/joystick (linux/SDL_sysjoystick.c, SDL_joystick.c, controller_list.h, SDL_gamepad_db.h)
  https://github.com/RetroPie/EmulationStation/blob/stable/es-core/src/InputManager.cpp
-->
